ietf-mib: also read the line tables indexed from 0

Some RFC 1628 agents (an RTCS 03.02.00 card, for one) number the
upsInputTable, upsOutputTable and upsBypassTable rows from 0 instead of 1,
so the single-phase voltages, currents, powers and load were never
published. Read index .0 as well. Whichever instance does not answer is
disabled at startup, and the .1 entry stays last so that it wins on an
agent answering both.

Upstream: not submitted yet.

